# Line endings for files that run somewhere other than here.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which stores
# CRLF in the blob for these files. That is harmless for Python, which does not
# care, and fatal for everything in deploy/: a shell script whose first line is
# `set -euo pipefail\r` fails on Linux with "$'\r': command not found", and a
# systemd unit with CRLF is parsed unpredictably.
#
# The deployment target is a Linux server, so these are pinned to LF regardless
# of the machine they are edited on. tests/test_deploy_units.py asserts it, so a
# regression fails in the suite rather than at 06:00 on the server.

deploy/**       text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf

# Batch files must keep CRLF to run reliably under cmd.exe.
*.bat          text eol=crlf
